      "title": "Missing or Broken Localization Text in Self-Service Hub Chat Widget",
      "content_summary": "Addresses issues where UI elements in the Chat Widget fail to render localized text correctly, often due to race conditions during load. Provides workarounds for known product limitations regarding dynamic string loading.",
      "content_body": "If localized strings appear blank or in the wrong language within the Chat Widget, check the browser console for failed resource requests. This is frequently caused by a race condition where the widget initializes before the locale file fully downloads. As a temporary workaround, clear the browser cache and force a hard refresh to ensure the locale bundle is cached correctly. If the issue persists across multiple users, escalate to engineering as this may indicate a known product limitation in the current release. A permanent fix is delivered via the latest product patch, which synchronizes locale loading with widget initialization."
